The real question is, does it need to be more evil for experienced
players, or for newbies?

The task facing anyone who would rebalance the game right now is to make
sure you don't make it harder for new players.  It's hard enough, and
yet engaging enough; the balance is fine there.  But experienced players
who can snowplow through everything effortlessly?  Ah, THEN you need to
make it a little more evil.

The problem with a blind application of "better monster AI" is that
swarm monsters such as hill orcs/Mordor orcs/Uruk-hai are the obvious
candidates, yet they show up at low enough levels to only be a threat to
the aforementioned newbies... who aren't the ones who need more evil.

There is, of course, a solution.  But it's not as simple as everyone
here is painting it to be.

